      "text": "Jana walks one mile in 24 minutes. To find out how far she can walk in 10 minutes, we need to determine the additional time needed and then find the equivalent distance for that time.\n\nThe remaining time after 24 minutes is 10 minutes. Since Jana takes 24 minutes to walk one mile, the distance she can walk in 10 minutes would be calculated using a proportion. This can be set up as follows:\n\nLet’s call the distance covered in 10 minutes “x.”\n\n\\[\\frac{24 \\text{ minutes}}{1 \\text{ mile}} = \\frac{10 \\text{ minutes}}{x \\text{ mile}}\\]\n\nWe express 10 minutes over 10 as \\(\\frac{10}{10}\\) which simplifies to 1:\n\n\\[\\frac{24}{x} = 1\\]\n\nSolving for x:\n\n\\[x = 24\\]\n\nThus, the number of miles Jana will walk in 10 minutes is 24.0 miles.",
